Package: DebrisFlowRF
Type: Package
Title: Debris-Flow Triggering Prediction from Rainfall and Lightning Data
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Welfringer Théo
Maintainer: Welfringer Théo <theo.welfringer@gmail.com>
Description: Builds rainfall events from a 15-min rainfall time series,
    extracts the rainfall and lightning descriptors used by a pre-trained
    Random Forest model ('ranger' package), and predicts the probability of
    debris-flow triggering for full rainfall events. The example
    provided evaluates the model on complete events (the full event is known
    before being submitted to the model); the descriptor-extraction
    functions could in principle be reused to evaluate a growing event
    step by step, but this use case is not implemented or evaluated here.
License: MIT
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
    slider,
    terra,
    ranger,
    stats,
    graphics
RoxygenNote: 7.2.3
